IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `fk68-nouns`
IMPORT `fk68-cross-references`

-- Row il-68. TESTS THAT PIN THE READINGS of the four references of the three items: both limbs hold, how each was read, and the typed values the items rest on.
-- These pass: they say what was read from what. The assertions that a citation points at what it says are in fk68-tests-red.l4.

§ `Tests of the readings`

-- I1: what the citing words name, what the target prints, and which citations Amendment 19 touched.
#ASSERT `both limbs hold` (`reference: I1, section 14(2) to section 7(a)`)
#ASSERT `how limb (a) was read in` (`reference: I1, section 14(2) to section 7(a)`) EQUALS `read from an official instrument; the present wording is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`
#ASSERT `how limb (b) was read in` (`reference: I1, section 14(2) to section 7(a)`) EQUALS `read from an official instrument; the present wording is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`
#ASSERT (`citation: section 14(2) names section 7(a)`)'s `the section the citing words name` EQUALS "7"
#ASSERT (`citation: section 14(2) names section 7(a)`)'s `the subsection letter the citing words name` EQUALS JUST "a"
#ASSERT NOT ((`citation: section 14(2) names section 7(a)`)'s `Amendment 19 replaced the citing words`)
#ASSERT `the citation names the section as printed` (`citation: section 14(2) names section 7(a)`) (`section 7 as item 1 of Amendment 19 prints it`)
#ASSERT NOT (`the citation names a subsection the section has` (`citation: section 14(2) names section 7(a)`) (`section 7 as item 1 of Amendment 19 prints it`))
#ASSERT count ((`section 7 as item 1 of Amendment 19 prints it`)'s `its subsection letters`) EQUALS 0

-- I2: the list as SH 3072 printed it, the list as SH 3493 item 2 extended it, and the two sentences that point at section 1C.
#ASSERT `both limbs hold` (`reference: I2, section 29A(a) to section 1C(a)`)
#ASSERT `how limb (a) was read in` (`reference: I2, section 29A(a) to section 1C(a)`) EQUALS `read from an official instrument`
#ASSERT `how limb (b) was read in` (`reference: I2, section 29A(a) to section 1C(a)`) EQUALS `read from an official instrument; the present wording is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`
#ASSERT `both limbs hold` (`reference: I2, section 29C to section 1C(a)`)
#ASSERT `how limb (a) was read in` (`reference: I2, section 29C to section 1C(a)`) EQUALS `read from an official instrument`
#ASSERT `how limb (b) was read in` (`reference: I2, section 29C to section 1C(a)`) EQUALS `read from an official instrument; the present wording is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`
#ASSERT (`the pointer sentence in section 29A(a)`)'s `the section the sentence names` EQUALS "1C"
#ASSERT (`the pointer sentence in section 29C`)'s `the section the sentence names` EQUALS "1C"
#ASSERT count ((`the provisions section 1C(a) names, as SH 3072 printed them`)'s `the provisions named`) EQUALS 5
#ASSERT count ((`the provisions section 1C(a) names, as SH 3493 item 2 extended them`)'s `the provisions named`) EQUALS 7
#ASSERT NOT (`the list names the provision` (`the provisions section 1C(a) names, as SH 3072 printed them`) "section 9C")
#ASSERT NOT (`the list names the provision` (`the provisions section 1C(a) names, as SH 3072 printed them`) ((`the pointer sentence in section 29A(a)`)'s `the citing place`))
#ASSERT NOT (`the list names the provision` (`the provisions section 1C(a) names, as SH 3072 printed them`) ((`the pointer sentence in section 29C`)'s `the citing place`))

-- I3: the three percentages and whether each is text the Knesset printed for the provision.
#ASSERT `both limbs hold` (`reference: I3, the 2023 instruction to section 13B(1)`)
#ASSERT `how limb (a) was read in` (`reference: I3, the 2023 instruction to section 13B(1)`) EQUALS `read from an official instrument; the present wording is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`
#ASSERT `how limb (b) was read in` (`reference: I3, the 2023 instruction to section 13B(1)`) EQUALS `read from an official instrument; whether a later instrument touched the words was not read`
#ASSERT (`the percentage the 2023 instruction quotes`)'s `the percentage` EQUALS 164.87
#ASSERT (`the percentage printed in section 3 of the order`)'s `the percentage` EQUALS 164.87
#ASSERT (`the percentage printed by Amendment 30`)'s `the percentage` EQUALS 116.3
#ASSERT (`the percentage printed by Amendment 30`)'s `the text printed by the Knesset for the provision` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`the percentage printed in section 3 of the order`)'s `the text printed by the Knesset for the provision` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`the percentage the 2023 instruction quotes`)'s `the text printed by the Knesset for the provision` EQUALS NOTHING
